# Make chargen.keys' orc barbarian and put a Circlet of Blasting on his head.
# Included by yuse-activate-blast.keys and a-activate-blast.keys, which differ
# only in which command they then use to activate it. bd inc-azc.
#
# The character owns nothing that blasts, so the item is made in wizard mode:
#
#   w y                      enter wizard mode and open its menu
#   Item Acquisition         the acquisition browser
#   RIGHT*19                 walk the glyph row to Headbands. ItemGlyphs
#                            (src/Tables.cpp:320) puts -AI_HEADBAND 19 steps
#                            along, and the header line names the category, so
#                            a miscount shows up in a dump as some other word
#                            after "Acquisition -- [...]:".
#   @until ... DOWN          the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#                            cursor is walked instead. The window shows three
#                            rows and highlights the middle one, so the run
#                            stops on the pass where the row BELOW the wanted
#                            one first appears. That is an ordering assumption
#                            about lib/m_items.irh, and the check does not
#                            trust it: tools/check_yuse_activate.sh reads the
#                            item's name back off the activate menu before
#                            believing anything else.
#   ENTER q SPACE ENTER      take it, put it in the helmet slot, leave the
#                            inventory manager. SPACE is the swap
#                            (src/Managers.cpp:873); the manager refuses to
#                            close while anything is still in the air.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*19
@until "Headband of Tactical Combat" DOWN
ENTER
q
SPACE
ENTER
